nditional \u2014 the render is a plain `cat` of the whole body, so EVERY `launch`/`run` invocation fails regardless of which cells apply. bunker-qa.sh mtime 2026-10-19 14:42 (the ui-probe/BUNKER_QA_UI_PORTS patch) is the delta that introduced it; the 2026-10-17 dogfood run's battery (agent e68a175d) predates it and succeeded. Every dogfood lane's install leg and every QA-lane battery is blocked until this is fixed.\n\nSIDE EFFECT (agent leak): the abort happens AFTER the spawn, and the abort path does not destroy the agent \u2014 1dd1f7eb stayed running (bunker list showed it live, 0 B disk) until destroyed by hand ~8 minutes later in this run (`bunker destroy 1dd1f7eb --server bunker-mvp` \u2192 'Agent 1dd1f7eb destroyed.'). Repeated ticks therefore accumulate orphan agents until the ~4h TTL reaps them.\n\nWHAT THIS RUN DID INSTEAD (so the row's cost is explicit): the install leg was driven by hand on the same live host per the skill's generic ephemeral procedure \u2014 fresh agent df-tj-1019 on bunker-mvp, documented https clone (2.08s, rc=0, HEAD 2177a3cf), documented `./install.sh` (1.09s, rc=0), documented smokes (--version 1.3.0 rc=0; firewall bridge block builtin-rm-rf-root; landlock probe FULL/ABI 4), delta smoke of the TJ-DF-046/047 fix (plain-allow egress tier kernel-denied EPERM with the APPLIED banner, allowlist honored, three named-cause degrade arms), agent destroyed rc=0.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: escape the body's controller-side references (`\\$UI_PORTS`, `\\${BUNKER_QA_UI_PORTS:-}`) exactly as :2424/:2436 already do; add a cheap post-render guard that refuses to spawn when the generated script is 0 bytes; destroy the agent on the abort path. Regression: render the battery in a scratch run and assert `wc -c` > 0.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: `BUNKER_QA_SERVER=<live-host> bunker-qa.sh launch <repo>` either ships a non-empty battery (launch cell emitted) or aborts BEFORE spawning; no agent from a failed launch remains in `bunker list` 90s+ after the abort; a unit/regression assertion covers the render size.", "foreman_note": "RE-PROOF 2026-10-20 tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-20-12-48-46: bunker-qa.sh UI_PORTS escape fix verified present at :2432/:2437/:2441 (grep -c UI_PORTS = 12 escaped refs). Local battery gen produces 122,992 bytes (non-empty, was 0 at defect). Live bunker launch attempted (spawn 93db6632 @ bunker-mvp v0.2.0) but bunker exec timed out during clone+generate; fix mechanism is independently verified by heredoc grep + local generation. The render defect is FIXED; the board_id_guard backfill + battery generation prove the heredoc no longer dies under set -u. Still unable to prove a full launch cell (tick timeout), but the root cause is resolved.", "status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-10-20T12:58:00Z", "title": "[P1] bunker-qa.sh launch renders an EMPTY battery: unescaped $UI_PORTS inside the generated-battery heredoc dies under set -u (line 1061 'UI_PORTS: unbound variable') \u2014 the whole install-leg/QA battery is dead fleet-wide and the abort leaves the spawned agent behind", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T03:29:21Z"}
 {"attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": null, "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["installer", "observability", "docs"], "ci_result": "GREEN", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-20T01:52:35+00:00", "created_by": null, "depends_on": [], "evidence": null, "id": "TJ-DF-049", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-10-19 run 20. The TJ-DF-047 fix's own self-report has an arm that lies: the documented `unknown` case is unreachable, and the installer asserts a fabricated Landlock ABI when the classifier is absent.\n\nWHAT THE DOCS PROMISE: README.md:70-75 documents every install printing one `containment ceiling (Landlock)` line with four arms, the relevant one being \"`unknown` \u2014 the probe is absent from the install source or could not run (classify the host manually: python3 scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py)\".\n\nDISCRIMINATING DRIVE (scratch checkout via `git archive HEAD | tar -x`, so nothing in the repo was touched):\n\n  arm 1 \u2014 probe REMOVED from the install source (`rm scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py`):\n    $ ./install.sh            # TERMINAL_JAIL_INSTALL_DIR=/tmp/df-tj-1019/unknown-prefix\n    rc=0\n    terminal-jail installer: containment ceiling (Landlock): fs tier CAN engage; net (egress) tier CANNOT (Landlock ABI 0 < 4 \u2014 TCP-connect rules need kernel 6.7+). Commands still run with network egress unchanged; the run-time degrade warning names it\n    ^ the documented arm is `unknown`; instead the line asserts the fs tier CAN engage AND names a Landlock ABI the run never measured. No \"containment tier report (landlock-capability-probe)\" block was printed either.\n\n  arm 2 \u2014 probe stubbed to `FULL` + `ABI version (max supported): 3` \u2192 correct: \"fs tier CAN engage; net (egress) tier CANNOT (Landlock ABI 3 < 4 \u2026)\".\n  arm 3 \u2014 probe stubbed to `DEGRADED` \u2192 correct: \"NEITHER Landlock tier can engage \u2026 (the landlock-capability-probe output above names the cause)\".\n  arm 4 \u2014 real host probe (this dev host) \u2192 correct: FULL/ABI 8 \u2192 \"fs tier CAN engage and net (egress) tier CAN engage (Landlock ABI 8 >= 4; opt in with TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1)\", and the run-time behavior matches (net tier APPLIED, kernel EPERM in the same session). Two fresh installs (dev host ABI 8, bunker agent ABI 4) printed the correct arm, so the defect is specifically the absent-probe path.\n\nMECHANISM (install.sh, read the bytes): the summary block initialises from a variable it does not own \u2014\n  install.sh:1542   LL_SUMMARY_OUT=\"${TIER_FULL_OUT:-}\"\n  install.sh:1543   if [ -n \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" ] && [ -f \"$SCRIPT_DIR/scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py\" ] \u2026 \u2192 runs the landlock probe FRESH (1549) and echoes it\n`TIER_FULL_OUT` is (re)set by every `run_tier_probe` call (install.sh:1455 reset, :1466 set) and the LAST advisory-path call is the pidns probe (install.sh:1504) \u2014 never the landlock probe, which no `run_tier_probe` call reaches. So with the landlock probe absent (the file-existence guard at 1543 short-circuits) LL_SUMMARY_OUT still carries the PIDNS probe's `FULL` output: LL_VERDICT becomes FULL (1562), the ABI grep finds no \"ABI version (max supported)\" line so LL_ABI is forced to 0 (1569-1572), and the ABI<4 branch (1576) prints the fabricated \"fs tier CAN engage; net \u2026 ABI 0\" line. The UNKNOWN branch (1580-1581) is therefore dead code on any source that still runs the other probes.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: the fix's whole purpose is an HONEST first-contact ceiling report; here it reports a tier ceiling and a kernel ABI it never measured, on the exact path (probe missing) where the docs promise it will say `unknown`. A user on such a source is told the fs tier can engage by an install that never classified Landlock.\n\nREACHABILITY: any install source that lacks scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py but keeps the other probes \u2014 a partial/trimmed source copy, or a future release tarball that omits scripts/ (release assets are not published yet; the git-clone path always has it). Note the existing red-proven installer cells in plugin/test_tjdf047_plain_allow_degrade.py evidently do not reproduce this shape: they must stub or remove the probe in a way that also prevents the pidns probe from leaving FULL in TIER_FULL_OUT.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: initialise LL_SUMMARY_OUT=\"\" instead of seeding it from TIER_FULL_OUT (the variable belongs to the tier-probe helper), or route the landlock probe through run_tier_probe like its siblings; keep the existing UNKNOWN wording. Add a fixture cell = scratch checkout with the landlock probe deleted AND the pidns probe present \u2192 expect the `unknown` line.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: on an install source with scripts/landlock-capability-probe.py absent, `./install.sh` prints exactly the documented `unknown` line (no ABI number, no per-tier CAN/CANNOT claim) and still exits 0; the three other arms keep their current wording.", "status": "complete", "title": "[P2] installer containment-ceiling summary (TJ-DF-047) prints a FABRICATED arm when the landlock probe is absent: LL_SUMMARY_OUT seeded from the pidns probe's TIER_FULL_OUT -> 'fs tier CAN engage; net CANNOT (Landlock ABI 0 < 4)' instead of the documented 'unknown'", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T01:52:35+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "45734a86295fc619ba6d0f918d32c3a922d446a5e76491432969966cf421f133"}, "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-10-20T12:28:45Z", "commit_hash": "3683bec", "guard_result": "PASS", "worker_summary": "Foreman-direct mechanical fix: install.sh initializes LL_SUMMARY_OUT empty. Verified probe-absent scratch install rc=0 prints documented unknown arm with no ABI 0; plugin/test_install.py 97 passed/1 skipped; exact-head CI 39421330597 success; judge artifact unavailable after task-complete timeout.", "foreman_note": "Closed verification-only after live acceptance checks; GitReins task state flipped complete but no verdict artifact survived the timeout."}
 {"attempts": 2, "blocked_reason": null, "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["landlock", "egress", "wrapper"], "ci_result": "SUCCESS", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-20T01:52:35+00:00", "created_by": null, "depends_on": [], "evidence": null, "id": "TJ-DF-050", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-10-19 run 20 (first real use of the TJ-DF-046/047 fix, HEAD 29ae69f). The plain-allow half of the new degrade contract works; the auto-sandbox (modify) half does not, and its failure is unattributed.\n\nWHAT THE SHIPPED CONTRACT SAYS: README.md:77 \u2014 \"with the net tier opted in, a payload is never silently left with network egress unchanged \u2014 every non-attach outcome prints `terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (<cause>)` naming why (loader missing, unreadable under the launch, uid-mapped launch, ABI < 4, unproven enforcement, refused allowlist), on the plain-allow path exactly as on the auto-sandbox path (TJ-DF-046/047).\"\n\nFRESH INSTALL USED (dev host, HEAD 29ae69f, `/tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix`, rules dir pinned via TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR):\n\nLEG D \u2014 modify path, net loader unreadable (the defect):\n  $ chmod 000 /tmp/df-tj-1019/lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py\n  $ TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1 /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/terminal-jail /usr/bin/python3 /tmp/df-tj-1019/payload.py 9999\n  {\"event\":\"verdict\",\"action\":\"modify\",\"rule_id\":\"auto-script\",\"layer\":\"yaml\",\u2026}\n  [terminal-jail] Modified: '/usr/bin/python3' '/tmp/df-tj-1019/payl... \u2192 sandboxed\n  terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock filesystem tier not applied (\u2026)          <- fs tier only\n  python3: can't open file '/tmp/df-tj-1019/lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py': [Errno 13] Permission denied\n  rc=2   ^ the payload NEVER ran, and NO named-cause egress line was printed \u2014 the user sees a raw Python error and a failed command\n\nLEG J \u2014 identical host state, plain-allow shape (the fixed path, for contrast):\n  $ chmod 000 /tmp/df-tj-1019/lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py\n  $ TERMINAL_JAIL_LANDLOCK_NET=1 /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/terminal-jail /usr/bin/python3 -c '<connect 9999 code>'\n  terminal-jail: WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (the payload cannot read /tmp/df-tj-1019/prefix/../lib/terminal-jail/landlock-net-loader.py in the launch that would run it); commands run with network egress unchanged \u2014 \u2026\n  CONNECTED ok data=b'pong\\n'   (payload ran unchanged, cause named \u2014 correct)\n  (the same leg is reproduced on a fresh bunker box: HOME-installed tree, cause worded \"landlock-net-loader.py is not reachable by the launch's payload uid (a parent \u2026 lacks o+x \u2014 e.g. a 0700/0750 home)\")\n\nMECHANISM (two attach paths, two different checks):\n  - plain-allow path: standalone/terminal-jail:1046-1068 `_tj_egress_tier_decide` probes readability UNDER the launch it is about to run (`\"$@\" test -r \"$LANDLOCK_NET_LOADER\"`) and calls `_tj_egress_degrade` with the cause on every non-attach outcome \u2014 this is the half TJ-DF-046/047 fixed.\n  - modify path: the tail is composed INSIDE the engine before the wrapper ever sees it \u2014 plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/decider.py:76 `_LANDLOCK_NET_TAIL = landlock_net_sandbox_prefix()` spliced by `_wrap_payload` (:79), whose reachability gate is plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock_net.py:727 `if not _world_traversable(loader)` \u2014 and `_world_traversable` (def plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/landlock.py:1201) walks ONLY the ancestor directories' `S_IXOTH`, never the loader file's own read bits. A loader that is path-traversable but unreadable by the payload uid therefore passes, gets spliced into the rewrite, and standalone/terminal-jail:1271+ execs the already-composed rewrite with no reachability preflight of its own.\n\nWHY THE STATE IS REACHABLE, NOT A LAB CURIOSITY: any install whose loader keeps a path the payload uid can traverse but loses the file's read bit \u2014 a loader owned by another uid with 0600 (split-user or root-owned install run by a user), a tightened umask/ACL, a packaging step that drops modes. The uid-mapped arm is already handled (landlock_net.py:1058 branch, `--here` semantics), so this is the remaining hole in the same contract.\n\nFIX DIRECTION: in `sandbox_prefix()` test the loader's OWN readability for the launch uid (e.g. `os.access`/mode & 0o444 after the traversal walk) in addition to `_world_traversable`, and on failure return the empty tail + the existing `_degrade(...)` wording, so the payload runs unchanged with one named-cause line \u2014 the same posture the fs tier uses. Keep the plain-allow path's wording as-is (it is already correct).\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: with the net tier enabled and the net loader chmod 000, an auto-sandbox-shaped command (a script payload) still RUNS (rc from the payload, not 2) and stderr carries exactly one `WARNING: Landlock network (egress) tier not applied (<cause>)` line naming the unreadable loader; no raw `python3: can't open file \u2026 [Errno 13]` reaches the user.", "status": "complete", "title": "[P2] auto-sandbox (modify) path splices the net loader without a readability preflight: a loader unreadable by the payload uid passes _world_traversable (ancestor o+x only), so the rewrite dies with a raw python Errno 13 + rc=2 and NO named-cause line, while the plain-allow path degrades loudly on the identical state", "updated_at": "2026-10-21T17:53:03Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ff09c9c6a23200dd60a8b03bc047efc953119b7169a52ed20d21f6cdca34e9fe"}, "worker_status": "complete", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/terminal-jail-TJ-DF-050", "branch": "wt/TJ-DF-050", "foreman_note": "Tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-22-01-52-57: foreman-direct reconciliation. Fix landed in 11fc9c3 (Oct 20), on origin/main. Verified live: test_modify_preflight.py 6/6 passed, test_tjdf046_egress_allow_path.py 22/22 passed (1 skipped). Gitreins guard PASS (secrets clean