 {"id": "TJ-GAP-096", "title": "[P3] HOST git-config leak: core.hooksPath=/var/tmp/foreign-hooks (set 2026-10-22 15:48) shadows this repo's own .git/hooks, so prepare-commit-msg never runs and every commit silently loses the AGENTS.md-mandated Co-authored-by trailer", "status": "blocked", "priority": "P3", "created_at": "2026-10-22T22:20:00-05:00", "created_by": "terminal-jail-foreman", "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["git", "host-environment", "commit-hygiene"], "complexity": 2, "attempts": 0, "blocked_reason": "HOST-level, not a repo defect: the shadowing value lives in ~/.gitconfig (global core.hooksPath=/var/tmp/foreign-hooks; the repo has no local override) and the directory was created 2026-10-22 15:48 by another project's probe. A repo worker cannot fix it and must not delete another component's host state. UNBLOCK: whoever owns that probe removes the global core.hooksPath (or points it at ~/.hermes/hooks with the repo hook chain intact) and confirms `git -C /home/kara/terminal-jail config --get core.hooksPath` is empty from a clean shell.", "description": "Every commit made in this checkout runs /var/tmp/foreign-hooks/pre-commit instead of the repo's own hook chain: `git config --get core.hooksPath` -> /var/tmp/foreign-hooks, and that directory contains ONLY a pre-commit. The repo appends its trailer in .git/hooks/prepare-commit-msg, which is therefore never executed. Observed this tick: three independent wave workers each produced a trailer-less commit and each had to amend through `git -c core.hooksPath=$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/hooks`. The guard banner still prints, so the loss is silent.", "reasoning": "Found at tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-23-02-51-59: three of four wave workers independently reported that their first commit landed with no Co-authored-by trailer. Verified foreman-side: `git config --get core.hooksPath` -> /var/tmp/foreign-hooks, `git config --local --get core.hooksPath` -> empty, `ls /var/tmp/foreign-hooks` -> pre-commit only, dir mtime 2026-10-22 15:48:33 -0500. Consequence: AGENTS.md's mandatory trailer is silently skipped for every commit on this host, and the repo's commit-msg path is untested in practice. Mitigation used this tick: pass the trailer explicitly in the commit message body.", "detail": {"global_hooks_path": "/var/tmp/foreign-hooks", "contents": ["pre-commit"], "dir_mtime": "2026-10-22T15:48:33-05:00", "shadowed_hook": ".git/hooks/prepare-commit-msg (appends the Co-authored-by trailer)", "observed": "4 of 4 wave worker commits this tick needed an explicit -c core.hooksPath override or a manual trailer"}, "updated_at": "2026-10-24T06:30:42Z", "acceptance_criteria": "`git config core.hooksPath` returns no value and `test ! -e /var/tmp/foreign-hooks/pre-commit` exits 0, proving the foreign global hook shadow no longer bypasses the repository trailer hook; current probe resolves to `/var/tmp/foreign-hooks`, so this remains owner-gated."}
 {"id": "TJ-GAP-097", "title": "[P1] Resident bridge daemon can hang forever at 100% CPU in accept() after SIGINT/SIGTERM: the signal handler closes the listening socket, then serve()'s `except OSError: continue` turns the closed-fd error into a busy loop \u2014 the process never exits and the property test burns its 30s budget waiting on a daemon that is alive and spinning", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "created_at": "2026-10-22T22:38:00-05:00", "created_by": "terminal-jail-foreman", "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["resident-bridge", "lifecycle", "signals", "resource-leak"], "complexity": 3, "attempts": 1, "blocked_reason": null, "description": "Observed live during this tick's post-merge full-suite gate on the merged main tree. pytest had been running 9 minutes with only 7s CPU and was blocked in anon_pipe_read; its child /home/kara/terminal-jail/.venv/bin/python plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py --serve --sock .../test_sigint_removes_socket0/s.sock had been in state R for 7:47 with 7:45 CPU consumed. py-spy (run as root) showed the main thread inside `accept (socket.py:294)` called from `serve (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py:241)` \u2014 i.e. the accept loop, after the signal handler had already closed `server` via _cleanup(). The handler's SystemExit never terminated the process, and the closed fd makes accept() raise OSError on every iteration, so `except OSError: continue` spins forever. Killing the daemon unblocked pytest.", "reasoning": "Found while gating the INT-CI-014 merge (tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-23-02-51-59). Evidence captured on the live process: /proc/<pid>/status 'State: R (running)', Threads 1, SigCgt 0x4002 (SIGINT+SIGTERM caught), 7:45 CPU in 7:47 elapsed; py-spy stack as above. Isolation control: the same 16-trial matrix (idle/mid-stream x SIGTERM/SIGINT, 4 trials each) run standalone with /tmp/tj_signal_spin_probe.py on an idle-ish box exits cleanly 16/16 (rc=143/130, socket removed every time), so the spin needs the loaded full-suite conditions \u2014 it is a race, not a deterministic path. Consequence for INT-CI-014: the hosted py3.13 'runner stall' (30s timeout, daemon alive) is very likely THIS spin, not a slow runner, so the retry that INT-CI-014 added is diagnosability only \u2014 it does not and must not mask the hang (both attempts still fail on a spinning daemon). Fix direction: make the accept loop exit when the listening socket is gone (EBADF must break/raise, not continue), or have the handler exit the process directly after cleanup, and add a regression test that the daemon is gone within a bounded time after a signal under load.", "detail": {"evidence_run": "tick terminal-jail-foreman-2026-10-23-02-51-59 post-merge gate", "process_state": "State: R (running), Threads: 1, SigCgt: 0000000000004002", "cpu_at_observation": "7:45 CPU / 7:47 elapsed", "py_spy_stack": ["accept (socket.py:294)", "serve (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py:241)", "main (plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor_resident.py:412)"], "isolation_control": "16/16 clean exits standalone (/tmp/tj_signal_spin_probe.py); spin needs full-suite load", "related": ["INT-CI-014", "TJ-REVIEW-073", "INT-CI-012"], "acceptance": ["a signal delivered while the daemon is blocked in accept() exits the process with 128+signum within a bounded time (no busy loop)", "the accept loop cannot spin on a closed listening fd (EBADF breaks/raises rather than continue)", "regression test drives the daemon under load and asserts exit + socket removal within the budget"]}, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "a623273 (worker) + ce7f0f8 (merge)", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN (run 39901804025 on 30f048d: py3.11/3.12/3.13 + lint + pip-audit + drift guards all success)", "judge_verdict": "tier2 None / tier1 None \u2014 record 61d47549", "worker_summary": "The accept loop no longer treats a closed listening socket as transient: _accept_loop stops on EBADF/fileno()==-1/a set shutdown marker and exits 128+signum, while genuine transient errors still continue. Deterministic regression tests drive the loop with a scripted listener (EBADF stops, EINTR/ECONNABORTED still serves) and fail against the pre-fix loop.", "foreman_note": "Found mid-tick by the post-merge gate, not by a board row: a daemon sat in State R for 7:45 of CPU in 7:47 of wall time after SIGINT, py-spy parked in accept() from serve(), while pytest blocked on its pipe. 16-trial isolation matrix exits clean on an idle box, so the spin needs full-suite load \u2014 the fix is structural rather than timing-dependent. The worker disclosed that it could not prove WHY the handler's SystemExit lost the race; the marker covers that window and stderr names it if it ever fires.", "completed_at": "2026-10-22T23:41:35-05:00"}
